@startuml
title RuleSphere - Activity Diagram\n07. Protected Execution Evidence | UC-24
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFF0ED
skinparam activityBorderColor #496477
|Trace Capture|
start
:Receive asynchronous auditable execution evidence;
:Identify sensitive fields using bound schema metadata;
:Mask, tokenize or hash sensitive values\nincluding intermediate outcomes, output and errors;
if (Protection succeeded?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Block unprotected persistence;
  :Report capture degradation and apply failure policy;
  stop
endif
fork
  :Attempt to persist full protected trace tree;
  :Collect hot-store success / failure / timeout;
  note right
Hot trace retention: configured 30-90 days.
end note
fork again
  :Build immutable compliance metadata;
  note right
ExecutionID, DecisionVersion, InputHash,
protected Output, MatchedNodeIDs, Timestamp,
approval/release evidence reference.
end note
  :Attempt to persist compliance metadata;
  :Collect ledger success / failure / timeout;
  note right
Ledger retention: configured 5-7 years.
end note
end fork
if (Both persistence attempts succeeded?) then (yes)
  :Record capture success;
else (no)
  :Report affected execution, failed store and degradation;
  :Apply operational retry / backpressure policy;
endif
stop
legend bottom
  This activity runs independently of the consumer response; its join only joins capture tasks.
  Persistence failure must not silently change the business decision outcome.
  Retry, timeouts, reliable delivery and backpressure details require ADR.
  Never store plaintext sensitive fields in execution traces.
endlegend
@enduml
